From 1cab2699ba4d2ff1ab3a4b6de10a1e798ad7ea1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 07:42:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Pi compat: compact, grouped, path-free extension diagnostics;
 one-line start failures

Adapter notices name the extension (never a path), give one reason and one
action, group identical problems, cap at four lines and split blocking
errors from warnings. Background errors are one line, once. The host
compacts 'did not start' reasons and drops scheduler jargon from queued
extension action notices. Rust part not yet compiled at this commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SJg4KTSPzhSXgwjtDWqAnQ
